{% comment %}
  Formatting for the quote under the reviews wave.

  The quote is its own section in templates/index.json with no shared wrapper
  with the wave above it, so the rules below are scoped from the wave that
  opens the run:

    .shopify-section:has(.wave-divider)   the wave
    + .shopify-section                    the quote

  That assumes the two stay adjacent and in that order. If they're reordered or
  something is inserted between them the styling drops off rather than landing
  on the wrong section - worth knowing, but it won't break the page.

  The "Reviews ·" label itself is no longer a section: it's set along the inside
  of the curve in wave-divider.liquid, so there are no marquee rules here.

  Rendered from the wave section's custom Liquid block, next to the divider.
  Wording is untouched; this only changes how it's set.
{% endcomment %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .shopify-section:has(.wave-divider) + .shopify-section .section-content-wrapper > *:first-child {
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* Attribution: smaller, dimmer and tracked out a little, so the quote is
     clearly the thing being read and this is the footnote to it. The rule
     above it separates the two without relying on space alone. */
  .shopify-section:has(.wave-divider) + .shopify-section .section-content-wrapper > *:last-child {
    opacity: 0.62;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .shopify-section:has(.wave-divider)
    + .shopify-section
    .section-content-wrapper
    > *:last-child::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1px;
    margin: 0 auto 0.9rem;
    background: currentColor;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
